INGRESS
Ingress is a Kubernetes object that defines how external traffic reaches services inside the cluster.
             or
Ingress is a Kubernetes API object that manages external HTTP/HTTPS access to services running inside the cluster. 
It acts as a centralized routing layer where we define rules such as host-based routing, path-based routing, SSL termination, and traffic redirection.

Instead of exposing every application using separate LoadBalancers, we use Ingress to expose multiple services through a single entry point.

example:
Internet User-->Route53-->ALB-->AWS Load Balancer Controller-->Ingress-->Service-->pods 
app.company.com/api     --> api-service
app.company.com/web     --> web-service
admin.company.com       --> admin-service


Ingress Controller
Kubernetes itself doesn't create load balancers.
An Ingress Controller watches Ingress resources and creates the actual load balancer.
              or
Ingress itself is just a configuration object; it cannot process traffic. 
An Ingress Controller is the actual component that watches Ingress resources and implements the routing rules.

The Ingress Controller continuously monitors the Kubernetes API server and creates the required load balancer configurations based on the Ingress definitions.

Examples:
Ingress Controller                 Creates
NGINX                     	       NGINX Load Balancer
Traefik                            Traefik LB
AWS Load Balancer Controller	     AWS ALB
HAProxy	                           HAProxy LB

Prerequisites
